          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Breastfeeding is generally beneficial for babies, providing essential nutrients and fostering emotional bonding. However, certain situations can make breastfeeding less ideal. For example, if a mother is taking specific medications, such as those mentioned in the retrieved passages, these drugs might pass into breast milk and potentially harm the baby. Additionally, some health conditions or medications can suppress lactation or lead to adverse effects. It\u2019s always best to consult a healthcare professional to evaluate individual circumstances and ensure the safety of both mother and baby.",
          "citations": {
