      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! Do you know if I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "During pregnancy, it\u2019s important to adjust your diet to meet the increased nutritional needs for both you and your baby. Key nutrients to focus on include calcium, protein, folic acid, and iron. Calcium is especially crucial for the development of your baby\u2019s bones and teeth, and it also helps prevent bone loss in the mother. Including calcium-rich foods like dairy products, leafy greens, and fortified alternatives can help address your concern about calcium intake. Protein is essential for fetal growth, and low-carb, high-protein options like tofu, eggs, and lean meats align well with your dietary preferences. Additionally, folic acid is vital for preventing neural tube defects, so incorporating foods like spinach, legumes, and fortified cereals is beneficial. \n\nYou may also need to increase your calorie intake slightly, especially in the second and third trimesters, but focus on nutrient-dense foods rather than empty calories. Avoid high-mercury fish, unpasteurized foods, and excessive caffeine. Consulting with a healthcare provider or dietitian can help tailor a plan to your specific needs.",
