          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, dietary adjustments during breastfeeding are important to ensure both you and your baby receive adequate nutrients. Breastfeeding increases your nutritional needs, particularly for protein, calcium, and certain vitamins like B12 and D. Since you\u2019re concerned about calcium intake, focus on calcium-rich foods such as dairy products, fortified plant-based milks, leafy greens, and almonds. Protein-rich options like lean meats, fish, eggs, and legumes are also beneficial, aligning with your preference for nutrient-dense foods. Additionally, staying hydrated is crucial, as breastfeeding can increase thirst.\n\nLow-carb foods can still fit into a breastfeeding diet, but ensure they include nutrient-dense options like avocados, nuts, seeds, and non-starchy vegetables. Avoid extreme dietary restrictions, as they may impact milk quality. If you feel your diet might lack certain nutrients, a multivitamin tailored for breastfeeding mothers could help, but consult your healthcare provider before starting any supplements.\n\nUltimately, a balanced, varied diet will support your baby\u2019s growth and your own health during this period. If you have specific concerns or dietary preferences, discussing them with a healthcare professional can provide personalized guidance.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0040-54-08630:0": 25.930999755859375,
            "clueweb22-en0045-27-06850:7": 25.82229995727539
