      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s useful! Is it possible for someone to run out of milk when they are breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can someone run out of milk when they are breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "It is unlikely for someone to completely run out of milk while breastfeeding, but milk supply can decrease due to various factors. Breast milk production works on a supply-and-demand basis, meaning the more frequently and effectively milk is removed from the breasts, the more milk is produced. Factors like infrequent feeding, poor latch, stress, or certain medical conditions can impact milk supply. However, even if milk production slows, it can often be increased with proper management, such as feeding on demand, ensuring effective milk removal, and addressing any underlying issues. Consulting a lactation consultant or healthcare provider can provide tailored advice to support milk production.",
