      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Good info, thanks! I try to avoid eating a lot of carbs\u2014are there good low-carb, calcium-rich foods I can eat? I\u2019m not a huge fan of milk.",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Great low-carb, calcium-rich options include green leafy vegetables (like kale and spinach), broccoli, okra, and calcium-set tofu. Nuts and seeds\u2014especially almonds and chia seeds\u2014are also good sources of calcium and low in carbohydrates. Fatty fish such as salmon and sardines (with bones) provide both calcium and omega-3s, which are beneficial during pregnancy. Fortified plant milks (like unsweetened almond or soy milk) and calcium-fortified foods can also help boost your intake without adding many carbs. If you find it difficult to meet your calcium needs through food alone, a calcium supplement (preferably calcium citrate) may be recommended, but always consult your healthcare provider before starting supplements. These options allow you to maintain a low-carb diet while supporting your calcium needs during pregnancy [clueweb22-en0040-56-10218:12][clueweb22-en0005-08-01400:10][clueweb22-en0035-79-07034:1].",
