          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Can someone run out of milk when they are breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can someone run out of milk when they are breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Most women are able to produce enough milk for their babies, and true inability to make enough milk is uncommon. Low milk supply can be caused by factors such as delayed breastfeeding after delivery, poor attachment, infrequent feeding, certain medical conditions, or previous breast surgery [clueweb22-en0021-55-01275:1][clueweb22-en0037-76-04586:3]. Sometimes, mothers may think they have low supply when their milk production is actually normal, as normal baby behaviors like frequent feeding or cluster feeding can be mistaken for signs of insufficient milk [clueweb22-en0026-25-06744:0]. Milk production works on a supply-and-demand basis, so feeding or expressing milk more often can help increase supply if needed [clueweb22-en0025-48-13143:1]. If you are concerned about your milk supply, monitoring your baby's weight gain and diaper output is a good way to check if they are getting enough milk. How can I increase my breast milk supply naturally?",
