          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "During breastfeeding, your body needs more energy, protein, calcium, and other micronutrients to produce high-quality breast milk and maintain your own health. Recommended intakes for most nutrients are 10\u201390% higher than for non-pregnant, non-lactating women, especially for protein and calcium, which are crucial for both you and your baby. If your diet is lacking, your body may draw on its own nutrient stores, which can affect your health over time. It's important to eat a balanced, nutrient-rich diet and consider foods like dairy, eggs, and lean proteins. While most foods are safe, you should be cautious with certain medications and substances, as they can pass into breast milk. Overall, a well-balanced diet helps ensure both you and your baby get the nutrients you need during this important period [clueweb22-en0010-41-08246:1][clueweb22-en0007-21-05565:1][clueweb22-en0007-21-05565:2]. Are there specific foods I should avoid while breastfeeding?",
