          "user_utterance": "I have a question about breastfeeding. Is it bad for babies?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Breastfeeding is not bad for babies\u2014in fact, for most mothers and infants, it is the healthiest choice.\n\n**Key Benefits for Babies:**\n- Reduces risk of infections (respiratory, diarrhoea), diabetes, certain cancers, and SIDS (Sudden Infant Death Syndrome).\n- Supports optimal nutrition and immune protection, especially in the first 6 months.\n\n**Key Benefits for Mothers:**\n- Lowers risk of breast cancer.\n- Supports postnatal weight loss.\n- Strengthens mother-child bonding.\n\n**When Breastfeeding May Not Be Safe:**\n- If the mother has certain medical conditions, takes specific medications, or uses harmful drugs (consult your healthcare provider if unsure).\n- Some infections and substances can pass through breast milk and harm the baby.\n\n**Lifestyle Factors:**\n- **Smoking:** Still better to breastfeed than not, even if you smoke, but cutting down or quitting is best. Breastfeeding can help protect your baby from some smoke-related risks.\n- **Alcohol:** Best avoided while breastfeeding, as it passes into breast milk and can affect your baby\u2019s",
