          "text": "You do not need a drastic diet change during pregnancy, but you do need to focus on a few key nutrients\u2014especially calcium, protein, and overall nutrient density, which aligns perfectly with your preferences.\n\n**Calcium Needs**\n- Aim for at least 1,000 mg/day. This is crucial for your baby\u2019s bone development and to protect your own bone health (if intake is low, your body will draw calcium from your bones).\n- Top low-carb, high-calcium foods: cheese, plain Greek yogurt, sardines (with bones), tofu (calcium-set), and leafy greens like kale and bok choy. Fortified plant milks are a good option if you avoid dairy.\n\n**Protein & Nutrient Density**\n- Increase protein intake (lean meats, eggs, fish like salmon and sardines, tofu, legumes).\n- Focus on nutrient-rich, low-carb foods: eggs (choline, B12), leafy greens (folate, vitamins A/C), nuts/seeds (zinc, selenium), seafood (omega-3s, iodine).\n\n**Supplements**\n- Most",
