          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "Here\u2019s what matters most for you during pregnancy and breastfeeding, given your focus on calcium, protein, nutrient density, and low-carb foods:\n\n**Foods to Strictly Avoid (Pregnancy & Breastfeeding):**\n- **Alcohol:** No safe level\u2014avoid entirely, as it can harm your baby\u2019s development and passes into breast milk.\n- **Certain Medications:** Some (like NSAIDs late in pregnancy) and specific prescriptions can be harmful\u2014always check with your doctor.\n- **Unpasteurized Dairy/Juices:** Risk of infection (listeria, etc.)\u2014choose only pasteurized products.\n- **Raw/Undercooked Meats, Eggs, Fish:** Infection risk\u2014ensure all animal products are fully cooked.\n- **High-Mercury Fish:** Avoid shark, swordfish, king mackerel; opt for low-mercury fish like salmon and sardines (which are also high in calcium and protein).\n\n**Foods to Be Cautious With:**\n- **Deli Meats, P\u00e2t\u00e9, Store-made Salads:** Can harbor bacteria\u2014eat only",
