          "user_rubrik": "Can someone run out of milk when they are breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Breast milk production is based on supply and demand. As long as the baby is nursing, the mother's body will continue to produce milk. It's rare for a mother to completely \"run out\" of breast milk, but milk production can decrease if the baby is not nursing frequently enough or if the mother is not getting enough rest and nutrition. If the baby is nursing regularly, the mother's body will adjust to meet the baby's needs, and milk production will increase accordingly. However, if the mother's body is not getting the necessary signals to produce milk, such as when the baby is not nursing or when the mother is taking certain medications, milk production can decrease or stop.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.   (I made the changes as per the suggestions)   However, I realized I made a mistake in the response. Here is the corrected response:  Breast milk production is based on supply and demand. As long as the baby is nursing, the",
