          "text": "Yes, it's possible for milk production to decrease or stop while breastfeeding. This can happen if you're not feeding your baby frequently enough, or if you're supplementing with formula too much. Additionally, hormonal changes, stress, or certain medical conditions can also affect milk production. If you're concerned about your milk supply, it's best to consult with your healthcare provider or a lactation consultant for personalized advice. They can help you identify the cause and provide guidance on how to increase your milk production if needed. In some cases, your body may naturally stop producing milk if you stop breastfeeding abruptly, but this can lead to engorged breasts or breast infections, so it's generally recommended to gradually wean your baby instead.",
          "citations": {
