      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Is breastfeeding ever harmful for a baby?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Breastfeeding has several benefits for the mother, including reducing stress and promoting nurturing behaviors. The hormones oxytocin and prolactin, released during breastfeeding, have antidepressant effects and can reduce anxiety. Breastfeeding can also help protect maternal mental health and reduce the risk of breast and ovarian cancer, type 2 diabetes, and high blood pressure. Furthermore",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0042-67-02541:9": 4.073571681976318,
            "clueweb22-en0023-53-04068:3": 3.544410228729248,
