          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that helps. Speaking of diet, do you know if I should change my eating habits if I get pregnant?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, it's a good idea to change your eating habits if you get pregnant. You'll want to focus on nutrient-dense foods, including plenty of fruits, vegetables, whole grains, lean proteins, and healthy fats. You may also need to limit or avoid certain foods, such as high-mercury fish or raw eggs. Additionally, you may want to consider taking a prenatal vitamin to ensure you're getting all the necessary nutrients for a healthy pregnancy. As someone interested in low-carb food, you may need to adjust your diet to ensure you're getting enough carbohydrates for your baby's development. It's always best to consult with your healthcare provider for personalized dietary advice during pregnancy.",
