      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Is breastfeeding ever a bad thing for a baby?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "No, breastfeeding is not a bad thing for a baby. In fact, it's a normal and healthy way for a baby to fall asleep and get comforted. Many babies nurse to sleep and wake up 1-3 times during the night for the first year or so. Breastfeeding can even help a child handle stress better when not breastfeeding. It's a way to nurture your child and can have a very positive effect on their physical and emotional well-being. So, don't be afraid to allow your baby to breastfeed to sleep. It's not a bad habit you've fostered, but rather a natural and comforting way for your baby to relax and fall asleep. Get all snug under the covers, and enjoy this special bonding time with your baby. External Resources: https://www.kellymom.com/bf/bfnewborn/sleep/comfortnursing.html https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/15-things-moms-pass-to-their-baby-through-bre",
