      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s more helpful! What about if the mother has health conditions, can that affect the baby through breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Yes, certain maternal health conditions, particularly those requiring specific medications, can affect the baby through breastfeeding. For instance, breastfeeding is not recommended if the mother is taking amphetamines, chemotherapy, ergotamines (for migraines), or statins (for high cholesterol). It's crucial for mothers on regular prescription medication to consult their doctor before breastfeeding.",
