      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting, thanks. Speaking of babies, do you know if a pregnant woman needs to change her diet at all?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, a pregnant woman needs to adjust her diet. She requires increased calories, especially in the second and third trimesters, and more nutrients. Focus on a balanced diet rich in fruits, vegetables, whole grains, lean proteins, and dairy for essential nutrients like folate, iron, calcium, and omega-3s. Daily prenatal vitamins with folic acid and iodine are recommended. Avoid raw or undercooked meats/seafood, unpasteurized products, high-mercury fish (e.g., shark, swordfish), alcohol, and limit caffeine. Prioritize hydration.",
