      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it. Are there any other situations where breastfeeding should be avoided?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Beyond previously mentioned drugs and health conditions, breastfeeding should also be avoided if the infant is premature or has hepatic immaturity. Other maternal conditions like HIV/AIDS, Ebola, HTLV-1, or Hepatitis C with cracked nipples are contraindications. Additionally, substances such as heroin, PCP, marijuana, excessive alcohol, tobacco, or ecstasy, and certain medications like aspirin or naproxen, also necessitate avoiding breastfeeding.",
