      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful. Do dietary needs change again after birth, when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, your dietary needs do change after birth, especially when breastfeeding. You'll require more calories and an increased intake of various nutrients. For calcium, which is crucial for both you and your baby's bones, aim for 1,000 mg daily (1,300 mg for teens). Good sources include dairy, fortified orange juice, kale, and broccoli. You also need more protein, iron, Vitamin C, B vitamins, omega-3s, folate, choline, iodine, and Vitamin D. Continuing your prenatal vitamins is often recommended.",
          "citations": {
