        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I see. Are there any common signs that someone isn\u2019t producing enough breast milk?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can someone run out of milk when they are breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Common signs a mother isn't producing enough breast milk include the baby losing more than 10% of their birth weight or not gaining enough weight. Look for insufficient wet or dirty diapers (e.g., dark urine, fewer than 6 wet/3 dirty by day 3). The baby may seem unsatisfied, cry constantly, have low energy, or be excessively sleepy. For the mother, breasts might remain firm after nursing or produce very little milk. If concerned, consult a healthcare provider.",
