      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that's clearer. Are there specific symptoms in infants that indicate something\u2019s wrong with breastfeeding, like allergic reactions or growth issues?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Symptoms in infants indicating breastfeeding issues, like allergic reactions or growth problems, can vary. Allergic reactions may present as gastrointestinal issues (vomiting, reflux, diarrhea, blood/mucus in stool, colic, gas), skin problems (rashes, hives, eczema, swelling of face/lips), or respiratory symptoms (wheezing, cough, nasal congestion). Behavioral signs include excessive crying, irritability, and fussiness. For growth issues, look for difficulty gaining weight or poor overall growth. If you observe these, consult a healthcare professional.",
          "citations": {
