      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! Is it safe to eat low-carb when breastfeeding, or could that affect my milk or the baby?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Low-carb diets are generally not recommended when breastfeeding. They can reduce your milk supply, as consistent energy from carbohydrates is vital. Rapid weight loss can also impact milk nutrition. Ketogenic diets are particularly concerning as it's unknown if ketones produced can harm the baby, and they may release toxins into breast milk. Such diets can also alter milk composition and hinder infant growth. Ensure adequate calorie intake (1800+ daily) and hydration. Always consult your doctor before making significant dietary changes.",
