      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful! What about nutrients\u2014can breastfed babies miss out on anything important, like calcium or protein?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Breastfed infants typically do not miss out on protein, as breast milk contains an ideal combination of proteins. While calcium is vital, breast milk levels of calcium are generally sufficient for the baby, even if the mother's intake is low. However, breastfed babies commonly need vitamin D supplements, as breast milk does not contain significant amounts of this vitamin. After about 4 months, breastfed babies may also need iron, and some may need vitamin B12 if the mother is deficient.",
