        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it! If I have to change my diet during pregnancy, what should I focus on for nutrients and protein?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "During pregnancy, focus on a balanced diet rich in essential nutrients. For protein, include lean meats, poultry, fish, eggs, dairy, and plant-based sources like beans, lentils, nuts, and soy products. Aim for about 75 grams daily.\n\nCalcium is crucial; aim for 1,000-1,300 mg daily. Excellent sources include milk, yogurt, cheese, dark leafy greens (kale, spinach), fortified foods (orange juice, cereals), and dried beans. If dietary intake is insufficient, your doctor may recommend a calcium supplement or prenatal vitamin.",
