          "user_utterance": "Interesting, thanks! What about foods\u2014do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, dietary changes are recommended during pregnancy. Focus on a balanced, nutrient-dense diet with increased intake of lean proteins, fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and dairy for calcium. Limit foods high in saturated fat, added sugar, and salt. Avoid raw/undercooked meats, high-mercury fish, and liver. Folic acid and iodine supplements are often advised. Consult your healthcare provider for personalized guidance.",
