    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "How about when breastfeeding? Should I keep eating more of certain nutrients like calcium or protein?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, it's important to maintain a nutrient-rich diet while breastfeeding, especially focusing on protein and calcium. Aim for at least 65 grams of protein daily from lean meats, fish, eggs, dairy, nuts, and legumes. For calcium, consume about 1,000 mg daily from dairy products, leafy greens, and fortified foods. Your body prioritizes your baby's calcium needs, potentially drawing from your own bone reserves, so adequate intake is crucial for your bone health. This temporary bone density loss is usually reversible after weaning.",
