          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s good to know, but is it possible for a mother to run out of milk completely when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can someone run out of milk when they are breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "While your breasts are never truly \"empty\" as milk is continuously produced, your overall milk supply can significantly decrease or even cease under certain conditions. Factors like infrequent feeding, not adequately emptying the breasts, or severe dietary restrictions can lead to a reduction in production. However, with consistent on-demand feeding, most mothers maintain an adequate supply.",
