      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s interesting, but I was hoping for more details\u2014are there any health problems for the baby that could come from breastfeeding itself?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "While breastfeeding offers many benefits, certain issues can lead to health problems for the infant. An insufficient milk supply can directly cause inadequate weight gain or even weight loss in the baby. Additionally, if a mother consumes foods or substances that the baby cannot tolerate, these can pass through breast milk and result in adverse reactions. Furthermore, prolonged separation from the mother during breastfeeding can cause significant distress and elevated stress levels in the infant.",
