        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Is it important to change my diet during pregnancy too, or is it okay to keep eating the same foods as before? I\u2019m especially interested in what foods might help with calcium and protein.",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, it's important to adjust your diet during pregnancy to support both your health and your baby's development. Focus on nutrient-dense foods. For protein, aim for about 70-75 grams daily from sources like lean meats, fish, eggs, beans, lentils, tofu, and nuts. For calcium, target 1,000-1,300 mg daily. Good sources include dairy products (milk, cheese, yogurt) and plant-based options like dark leafy greens, tofu, almonds, and fortified plant milks.",
