  {
    "runtag": "ucsc-SIMRAG-keywordQuery-dynamicPTKB-trainedReranker",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "5-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That helps a lot! Are there foods I should avoid when breastfeeding, especially things that could upset the baby\u2019s stomach or cause allergies?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To avoid upsetting your baby's stomach or causing allergies while breastfeeding, you might consider limiting or avoiding certain foods. Common culprits for fussiness, gas, or colic include dairy, citrus fruits (like oranges, tomatoes, strawberries), nuts, shellfish, caffeine, beef, corn, egg whites, and gassy vegetables (e.g., cabbage, broccoli, beans, lentils).\n\nFor babies with acid reflux, acidic, spicy, fatty/fried foods, peppermint, and carbonated beverages can be problematic. If your baby has eczema, consider avoiding common allergens like dairy, egg whites, shellfish, wheat, nuts, tomatoes, citrus, and soy. Limiting alcohol and artificial sweeteners is also advisable.",
          "citations": {
