        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it! Can what I eat while breastfeeding affect the taste of the milk? (I eat jam for breakfast a lot, so I\u2019m curious.)",
          "user_rubrik": "Can someone run out of milk when they are breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Yes, what you eat while breastfeeding can affect the taste of your breast milk. Your diet causes subtle changes in its flavor, which can expose your baby to a wider range of tastes. This exposure might even influence their acceptance of different foods when they start solids. While jam isn't specifically mentioned, the general principle applies to various flavors from your diet.",
