    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Is breastfeeding harmful to infants in any way?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is breastfeeding bad for the baby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "short answer : no \u2014 breastfeeding is not harmful. it \u2019 s the recommended, safest nutrition for infants and has many benefits. a few considerations to keep it safe and complete : - vitamin d : human milk is low in vitamin d. give your breastfed baby 400 iu ( 10 mcg ) vitamin d daily from birth through at least 12 months. - maternal nutrition : milk levels of calcium, iron, zinc, etc., are usually adequate even if your intake is low. calcium supplements help you, not baby. aim for 1, 000 mg calcium / day for yourself while breastfeeding. - b vitamins : some b vitamins ( especially b12 ) reflect your diet. if you eat no animal products, take b12. - medical exceptions : don \u2019 t breastfeed if baby has classic galactosemia. breastfeeding may be unsafe with certain maternal infections ( e. g., hiv in some settings ) or medications \u2014 ask your clinician. - feeding issues : poor latch or infrequent feeds can cause dehydration and poor weight gain ; jaundice can occur but is manageable. monitor diapers and weight. - substances : avoid smoking ; limit alcohol and time",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-72-17653:0": -2.4586446285247803,
            "clueweb22-en0040-54-08630:2": -4.045047760009766,
            "clueweb22-en0007-12-03679:3": -4.849653244018555,
            "clueweb22-en0012-93-02180:1": -4.865354537963867,
            "clueweb22-en0012-38-16947:1": -4.901271820068359
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
