      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting, thanks. So should my food choices be different while I'm pregnant? Do I need more of certain nutrients or should I avoid some foods?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet during pregnancy?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "yes \u2014 pregnancy changes your nutrient needs and a few food - safety rules matter. aim to get more of : - protein : about 70 \u2013 80 g / day. include eggs, poultry, fish, beans, lentils, tofu, greek yogurt. - folate / folic acid : 600 mcg / day ( prenatal vitamin covers this ). - iron : 27 mg / day ; pair iron - rich foods ( meat, beans, fortified cereal ) with vitamin c ( citrus, peppers ). - iodine : 220 mcg / day ( prenatal + iodized salt ). - dha omega - 3 : 200 \u2013 300 mg / day ( low \u2011 mercury fish or algae oil ). - choline : 450 mg / day ( eggs, lean meats, soy ). - calcium : 1, 000 mg / day + vitamin d 600 iu. good non \u2011 dairy options : calcium \u2011 fortified oj or oatmeal, canned salmon with bones, canned light tuna ( limit ), leafy greens, sesame seeds, sweet potatoes, figs. consider a calcium + d supplement if diet falls short. food choices and swaps : - choose whole grains more often ( brown rice",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0043-17-12288:9": -0.8763923645019531,
            "clueweb22-en0037-27-07241:4": -0.9475977420806885,
            "clueweb22-en0005-52-13253:4": -1.0664541721343994,
            "clueweb22-en0008-51-18045:11": -1.143369436264038,
            "clueweb22-en0043-17-12288:8": -1.339486837387085
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
