  {
    "runtag": "uva-gpt5-bm25-debertav3-gpt5mini-nopersonal",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "5-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What about breastfeeding\u2014do I need to eat differently once the baby is born?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do I need to change my diet when breastfeeding?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You don't need a special or restrictive diet while breastfeeding, but you should eat a varied, healthy diet and take a few simple precautions.  Practical points - Aim for a balanced diet: plenty of fruit and vegetables, whole grains, protein (meat, fish, eggs, pulses, nuts), dairy or calcium-rich alternatives, and healthy fats.   - You will need extra energy while breastfeeding, so eat nutrient-dense meals and snacks to maintain your supply and energy.   - Drink plenty of fluids\u2014keep a drink nearby when you feed.   - Take a daily vitamin D supplement (about 10 mcg) and consider continuing your prenatal vitamin if advised by your clinician.   - Limit alcohol and caffeine, avoid smoking and recreational drugs, and always check prescription or herbal medicines with your clinician before breastfeeding.   - If your baby seems unsettled after you eat a particular food, talk with your baby\u2019s doctor; a supervised elimination trial may help identify a cause without harming your nutrition.  If you have special dietary needs (vegan/vegetarian) or concerns, ask a clinician or nutritionist for tailored advice.",
          "citations": {
